{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgmn9DDwUJpqhJHdUikdm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I read all ten screenshots. The page shows three drawings of the same list: **\"1. החברה בראש השורה\"** (company at the top of each row), **\"2. קיבוץ לפי חברה\"** (grouped by company) and **\"3. טבלת חברות מול סוגים\"** (companies against investment types). The third has the designers' **\"מומלץ\"** (recommended) badge.\n\n## 1. My answer\n\nI'd pick **option 3, \"טבלת חברות מול סוגים\"**, and use the list under it, **\"כל המסלולים\"**, to check returns. I'm about 70% sure.\n\nI didn't pick it because of the \"מומלץ\" badge. I picked it because it was the only part where one row per company let me see who is cheap and who is expensive. The note says **\"כתום חזק יותר הוא דמי ניהול גבוהים יותר\"** (stronger orange means higher fees). That's plain enough even for me. The **מור** row is orange almost all the way across, at 0.67%–0.73%. The **הראל** row is dark, at 0.54%–0.61%.\n\nSo what does that mean for my money? If I had 200,000 ₪, the gap between 0.52% (מנורה) and 0.71% (מור) in the S&P 500 track is about 380 ₪ a year, every year. That I understand.\n\nWhat I'd actually do: shortlist הראל, מנורה and אלטשולר for an S&P 500 track. Then I'd phone them. I wouldn't move money based on this page alone.\n\n## 2. Parts I actually used\n- The top line: **\"143 מסלולים של 12 חברות… מנתוני רשות שוק ההון\"**. It told me the numbers come from the official regulator, the Capital Market Authority, so I trusted the page a bit more.\n- The **\"עוקב מדד s&p 500\"** button, to compare like with like.\n- The grid **\"כל החברות מול כל סוגי ההשקעה\"** in option 3.\n- In the list, the fee column **\"דמי ניהול, ממוצע 2025\"** and the return column **\"תשואה שנתית ממוצעת, לפני דמי ניהול\"**.\n- The note at the bottom of each list: **\"התשואה היא תשואת עבר… היא לא אומרת מה יקרה בהמשך\"** (past returns don't say what will happen next). I read it twice. It's honest, and it's the reason I lean on fees and not on returns.\n\n## 3. Block by block\n- **Title and the line about \"מספר אמיתי; אף מספר לא הומצא\"** (every number is real, none made up): read it. It reassured me.\n- **\"משותף לשלוש, ומה שהנתונים מראים\"** (shared by all three, and what the data shows): looks like a link. I didn't know what it would open, so I skipped it.\n- **The three option buttons and \"מחשב / טלפון\"** (computer / phone): used the option buttons. I ignored computer/phone.\n- **The bar \"מקור · מדריכים · חוקים וכללים · שאלות · חברות ומסלולים · השקעה במדד\"** (source, guides, rules, questions, companies and tracks, index investing): this confused me. It appears three times on one page, and I kept thinking I had scrolled back to the top.\n- **\"לפי חברה / לפי מוצר\"** (by company / by product): skipped. I wasn't sure what clicking would change.\n- **The product row (\"תגמולים ואישית לפיצויים 182\", \"קרן השתלמות 154\"…)**: I checked that **\"קופת גמל להשקעה\"** was selected and left the rest alone.\n- **\"במה הכסף מושקע\"** (what the money is invested in), the row of 19 buttons: skimmed it. I recognised **\"מניות\"** (shares), **\"כללי\"** (general) and **\"s&p 500\"**. **\"עוקב מדדים - גמיש\"**, **\"אג\"ח ממשלתי סחיר\"** and **\"מט\"ח\"** read as jargon to me.\n- **\"מיון לפי\"** (sort by): noticed it, didn't need it.\n- **\"חיפוש בשם המסלול\"** (search by track name): skipped.\n- **Option 1 list (S&P 500, one row per company)**: used it. Easy, because every row is the same kind of track.\n- **Option 2 (grouped by company: all 16 of הראל's tracks, then all 15 of מור's)**: skimmed, then gave up. It's very long, and comparing הראל with מור meant scrolling back and forth. I don't need 16 tracks from one company.\n- **Option 3 grid**: used it most.\n- **Note under the grid, \"סוגים עם פחות משבעה מסלולים מופיעים רק ברשימה\"** (types with fewer than seven tracks appear only in the list): fine.\n- **Orange notes starting \"✎ בשרטוט בלבד\"** (in the drawing only): I gathered they were notes from the designers, not for me. Skipped.\n\n## 4. Tables and columns\n**Looked at:**\n- **\"מתוך החיסכון\"** fee (fee taken from savings): the main number.\n- The 3-year and 5-year returns (\"3 שנים\", \"5 שנים\"). In the S&P track they're all about 13.3%–13.9%, so nearly the same everywhere. For me that pointed back to fees.\n- **\"נכסים בסוף ספטמבר 2026\"** (assets at end of September 2026): glanced at it to see whether a fund is big or tiny. 2 million ₪ for **איילון**, marked **\"חדש\"** (new), made me wary.\n- The orange shading in the grid.\n\n**Ignored:**\n- The **\"קופה\"** numbers (13874, 14865…). Meaningless to me.\n- **\"מתוך ההפקדות 0%\"** (fee from deposits). Almost always 0%, so I stopped looking.\n- The coloured rings, and the green **\"מניות\"** and yellow **\"מט\"ח\"** dots with percentages under **\"חשיפה\"** (exposure). I couldn't tell what 99% מט\"ח does to me.\n- The little clock icons and the dotted underlines. I didn't know if they were clickable.\n\n## 5. What I didn't understand\n- **\"חשיפה\"** with **\"מט\"ח 99%\"**: does that mean my money moves with the dollar? Is that good or bad for me?\n- **\"פחות מ־3 שנים\"** (less than 3 years): the track is too young to have a 3-year return? I guessed. Nobody told me.\n- **\"עוד לא דווח\"** (not reported yet), **\"חדש\"** and **\"—\"** in the grid: what's the difference between them?\n- **\"לפני דמי ניהול\"** (before fees): so what did people actually get? I had to do the subtraction myself.\n- **\"ממוצע 2025\"** (2025 average): average of what? Will I pay 0.56%, or can I get less?\n\n## 6. What I wanted and couldn't find\n- Return **after** fees: what actually reaches my pocket.\n- An example in shekels, like \"on 100,000 ₪ over 10 years, the difference between companies is X ₪.\"\n- How much a track lost in a bad year. At 61, that matters more to me than the average.\n- Whether I can bargain the fee down.\n- How to move money between companies, and whether moving costs anything or affects tax.\n- What happens at 60 and over: taking a monthly pension from it, and the tax rules.\n- Customer service. Will someone answer the phone?\n\n## 7. If half the page had to go\n1. The repeated bar **\"מקור · מדריכים · חוקים וכללים…\"** and the repeated **\"לפי חברה / לפי מוצר\"**: keep one at the top.\n2. **Option 2**, the long grouped list.\n3. The rings and the **\"מניות / מט\"ח\"** exposure percentages, or else explain them in plain words.\n4. The **\"קופה\"** number column and **\"מתוך ההפקדות\"**.\n5. Half of the **\"במה הכסף מושקע\"** buttons, the ones with fewer than three tracks.\n\nI'd keep the grid, the fee and return columns, and the **\"תשואת עבר\"** warning."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9052,"cache_read_input_tokens":12813,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9052},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"956afd30-f698-4ded-8467-a4376c8ed966","uuid":"d6fd9466-6ca1-41d9-94b8-4fa2a541e641","timestamp":"2026-11-06T13:48:37.244Z","request_id":"req_011Cgmn9Cw5NrZLW4rkb48PM"}
